From a0e99c05b3462bfae13bf1303f2595f3f41456e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:42:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(sim): the new-block-after-flip pin judges blocks that
 differ from above

The pin compared the program verdict (top - part per column) of the
carried run against the new-block run. Both starting stocks stood 60 x 60
with a Z18 top and differed only below the part, and Face2 faced both to
the part top, so both verdicts were exactly zero by construction. The
test failed on #408's own branch head as well; neither #410 nor the merge
caused it, and the sim's Entry::NewBlock path is correct.

The fixture now gives Setup2 its own 24 mm block (top Z22) and stops
Face2 at Z19. The carried run reads 2 mm of rest and the new block 3 mm.
Both values are pinned, along with the verdict difference and the
undo/redo round trip.

Fixes #415

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
